<title>POLAND: Polish NFI Piast makes Q1 PLN 0.4 mln net profit.</title>
<headline>Polish NFI Piast makes Q1 PLN 0.4 mln net profit.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Investment Fund (NFI) Piast (No. 12) in Poland's mass privatisation scheme made a net profit of 0.35 million zlotys in the first quarter of 1997, the fund said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>NFI Piast, which did not report results for the first quarter of 1996, made a net loss of 31.3 million zlotys for all of that year.</p>
<p>NFI Piast said its net assets amounted to 382.3 million zlotys in the first quarter of 1997. @</p>
<p>Under the government's NFI programme, shares in about 500 mid-sized companies are allocated to 15 NFIs run by foreign and domestic management firms.</p>
<p>Each NFI has 31,026,185 shares.</p>
<p>The units lose their validity on December 31, 1998.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
